{"assets":["/statement-assets/03dd2cd73fac9092c158a191fbeb7ca50025a0175b0bc1ad101ee3b36386e282.png","/statement-assets/084bd6329884f14b7ae37260018d3134f2993c5030ed87eda9897bb3d61aca54.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"690","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B2. Recover Polygon (medium)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now that Heidi has made sure her Zombie Contamination level checker works, it's time to strike! This time, the zombie lair is a strictly convex polygon on the lattice. Each vertex of the polygon occupies a point on the lattice. For each cell of the lattice, Heidi knows the level of Zombie Contamination – the number of corners of the cell that are inside or on the border of the lair."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given this information, Heidi wants to know the exact shape of the lair to rain destruction on the zombies. Help her!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/03dd2cd73fac9092c158a191fbeb7ca50025a0175b0bc1ad101ee3b36386e282.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input contains multiple test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains one integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":", the size of the lattice grid ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 ≤ N ≤ 500"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines each contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters, describing the level of Zombie Contamination of each cell in the lattice. Every character of every line is a digit between 0 and 4. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Cells are given in the same order as they are shown in the picture above: rows go in the decreasing value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinate, and in one row cells go in the order of increasing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinate. This means that the first row corresponds to cells with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, N), ..., (N, N)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the last row corresponds to cells with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 1), ..., (N, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last line of the file contains a zero. This line should not be treated as a test case. The sum of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" values for all tests in one file will not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5000"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, give the following output:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the output should contain one integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"V"},{"kind":"text","text":", the number of vertices of the polygon that is the secret lair. The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"V"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines each should contain two integers, denoting the vertices of the polygon in the clockwise order, starting from the lexicographically smallest vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n00000000\n00000110\n00012210\n01234200\n02444200\n01223200\n00001100\n00000000\n5\n00000\n01210\n02420\n01210\n00000\n7\n0000000\n0122100\n0134200\n0013200\n0002200\n0001100\n0000000\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n2 3\n2 4\n6 6\n5 2\n4\n2 2\n2 3\n3 3\n3 2\n3\n2 5\n4 5\n4 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the solution always exists and is unique. It is guaranteed that in the correct solution the coordinates of the polygon vertices are between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N - 2"},{"kind":"text","text":". A vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is lexicographically smaller than vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x2, y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1 < x2"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/084bd6329884f14b7ae37260018d3134f2993c5030ed87eda9897bb3d61aca54.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B2","problemCode":"690B2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/690/problem/B2"}